</Example>

<h2 class="doc-h2">As a palette</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    The search box in this site's header is this component, with the same shortcut.
</p>
<Example Source="CommandDialogExample.razor">
    <CommandDialogExample />
</Example>

<h2 class="doc-h2">Code block</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    Not shadcn's — it has none to export. Every <b>Code</b> tab on this site is this component.
</p>
<Example Source="CodeBlockExample.razor">
    <CodeBlockExample />
</Example>

<h2 class="doc-h2">When the list is too long to render</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    Filtering in the browser is right for a list the server already sent. For a catalogue of ten
    thousand, put <code>up-autosubmit</code> and <code>up-target</code> on the input and let the
    server answer — <code>&lt;CommandList&gt;</code> is the fragment it swaps. Same markup, and
    the palette never holds a list it did not need.
</p>
